Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: charge received airtime to the station deficit

The airtime a station spends transmitting to us is medium time taken from
everyone else, and the deficit scheduler expects both directions. The
monitor status ring already reports a per PPDU receive duration, which the
driver only accumulates for the station dump.

Register it with mac80211 as receive airtime for the same station and
TID.

This is a backport of patch 7/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
index 4c6aa82..b1bc292 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -5317,6 +5317,14 @@ int ath11k_dp_rx_process_mon_status(struct ath11k_base *ab, int mac_id,
 		arsta = ath11k_sta_to_arsta(peer->sta);
 		ath11k_dp_rx_update_peer_stats(arsta, ppdu_info);
 
+		/* The airtime a station spends transmitting to us is medium
+		 * time it took from everyone else, so charge it to the same
+		 * deficit the transmit airtime is charged to.
+		 */
+		if (ppdu_info->rx_duration && ppdu_info->tid < IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS)
+			ieee80211_sta_register_airtime(peer->sta, ppdu_info->tid,
+						       0, ppdu_info->rx_duration);
+
 		if (ath11k_debugfs_is_pktlog_peer_valid(ar, peer->addr))
 			trace_ath11k_htt_rxdesc(ar, skb->data, log_type, rx_buf_sz);
 
